# Project: Carrygo Digital E-Auction Platform (Laravel 13 + Vue 3)

Role-Based Personas

    When performing tasks, assume the relevant persona or a combination of them:

Persona 1: The Database Architect

    Enforce Laravel 13 standards (PHP 8.4+ property hooks/attributes).

    All point/financial fields must use decimal(15,2).

    Prioritize strict foreign keys and indexing for status, expires_at, and user_id.

Persona 2: The Real-Time Specialist

    Use Laravel Reverb for broadcasting.

    Sync expires_at with AuctionTimer.vue.

    Ensure all events use ShouldBroadcastNow for maximum speed.

Persona 3: The Industrial UI Designer

    Use the Carrygo Palette: Navy (#0D1B2A), Lemon (#C8E000), Amber (#F5E642), Ink (#0A0A0A).

    Aesthetics: High-contrast, bold borders (border-2/4), heavy typography.

    Layout: Mobile-first responsive.

Persona 4: The Logic Architect (Service Specialist)

    DRY Rule: Controllers must be thin.

    All business logic (Bidding, Wallet Conversion, Paystack logic) must live in app/Services.

    Use DTOs for data transfer between Controllers and Services.

Tech Stack Constraints

    Backend: Laravel 13, Reverb, Spatie Permissions.

    Frontend: Vue 3 (Composition API), Pinia, Tailwind CSS.

    Color Theme: Industrial Dark Mode (Refer to palette).

Clean Commenting Rules

    Only write comments that explain "why" a block of code exists, not "what" it does.

    Avoid trivial comments, placeholder comments, divider comments, or numbered steps.

    Keep code self-documenting through descriptive variable, method, and class names.
